    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          1
        ],
        "content": "## Turn podcast episodes from Google Drive into posts with Deepgram and Claude\n\nContent teams that publish one long piece and never get to the ten short ones it could become.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: A recording dropped in the 'episodes' folder, a new item in the podcast RSS feed, or a Riverside/Zoom recording webhook starts the run.\n1. Transcribe\n2. Extract structure\n3. Draft the long-form\n4. Draft the short-form\n5. Clip list for the editor\n6. Review board\n7. Schedule approved assets\n8. Report performance back\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Deepgram / AssemblyAI, Notion, Buffer / Hootsuite / CMS.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nSet the output formats and your voice rules in the Config node; publish through Buffer, Hootsuite or your CMS.\nGuardrail to keep: Nothing publishes without approval on the review board.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/content-repurposing-automation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
